/* Technical explanations and full interview-ready answers; preserve original progress IDs. */
if(typeof topics!=='undefined') { topics.push(...[{"id":"revision-extra-1","day":1,"title":"C# · Boxing and unboxing","concept":"A copy is wrapped in an object, usually allocating on the heap.","ar":"الـboxing بيعمل نسخة من الـvalue type داخل object، والـunboxing بيرجع نسخة بعد type check. لو ده بيتكرر في loops كتير هتزود allocations وضغط على الـGC. استخدم List<int> بدل ArrayList.","question":"What happens when you box a value type?","answer":"A copy is wrapped in an object, usually allocating on the heap.","code":"object value = 42; int number = (int)value;","category":"C#","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: A copy is wrapped in an object, usually allocating on the heap.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: Boxing copies the value into an object instance; unboxing performs a checked cast and copies it back. Repeated boxing in hot loops causes avoidable allocations and garbage collections. Generic APIs such as List<int> keep integers unboxed.\n\nExample: object value = 42; int number = (int)value;","arabic":"الـboxing بيعمل نسخة من الـvalue type داخل object، والـunboxing بيرجع نسخة بعد type check. لو ده بيتكرر في loops كتير هتزود allocations وضغط على الـGC. استخدم List<int> بدل ArrayList.","commonMistake":"Repeated boxing in hot loops causes avoidable allocations and garbage collections. Generic APIs such as List<int> keep integers unboxed.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Boxing and unboxing, and why?","answer":"Boxing copies the value into an object instance; unboxing performs a checked cast and copies it back. Repeated boxing in hot loops causes avoidable allocations and garbage collections. Generic APIs such as List<int> keep integers unboxed."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Boxing and unboxing.","answer":"الـboxing بيعمل نسخة من الـvalue type داخل object، والـunboxing بيرجع نسخة بعد type check. لو ده بيتكرر في loops كتير هتزود allocations وضغط على الـGC. استخدم List<int> بدل ArrayList."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-2","day":1,"title":"C# · Records and value equality","concept":"Records provide value-based equality and concise immutable-style data modeling.","ar":"الـrecord بيساعدك تعمل DTO أو Value Object بالمقارنة حسب القيم، وكمان with للنسخ. لكنه مش deep immutable تلقائيًا. الـEF entity غالبًا class لأن ليها identity ودورة حياة.","question":"When would you use a record rather than a class?","answer":"Records provide value-based equality and concise immutable-style data modeling.","code":"public record CustomerDto(int Id, string Name);","category":"C#","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Records provide value-based equality and concise immutable-style data modeling.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: Record classes synthesize equality by their values, deconstruction and with-expression copying; ordinary classes normally compare references unless equality is overridden. A record is not deeply immutable: mutable referenced collections can still change. Prefer classes for identity-driven EF entities.\n\nExample: public record CustomerDto(int Id, string Name);","arabic":"الـrecord بيساعدك تعمل DTO أو Value Object بالمقارنة حسب القيم، وكمان with للنسخ. لكنه مش deep immutable تلقائيًا. الـEF entity غالبًا class لأن ليها identity ودورة حياة.","commonMistake":"A record is not deeply immutable: mutable referenced collections can still change. Prefer classes for identity-driven EF entities.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Records and value equality, and why?","answer":"Record classes synthesize equality by their values, deconstruction and with-expression copying; ordinary classes normally compare references unless equality is overridden. A record is not deeply immutable: mutable referenced collections can still change. Prefer classes for identity-driven EF entities."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Records and value equality.","answer":"الـrecord بيساعدك تعمل DTO أو Value Object بالمقارنة حسب القيم، وكمان with للنسخ. لكنه مش deep immutable تلقائيًا. الـEF entity غالبًا class لأن ليها identity ودورة حياة."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-3","day":1,"title":"C# · IEnumerable vs IQueryable","concept":"IQueryable builds provider-translatable queries, while IEnumerable operates through enumeration.","ar":"الـIQueryable بيخلي EF يترجم Where وSelect لـSQL قبل التنفيذ. IEnumerable واجهة للتكرار ومش معناها إن البيانات اتحملت بالفعل. لكن ToList بتنفّذ الاستعلام؛ أي Where بعدها هتشتغل داخل التطبيق وهتستهلك نقل وذاكرة أكثر.","question":"Why does IQueryable matter when working with EF Core?","answer":"IQueryable builds provider-translatable queries, while IEnumerable operates through enumeration.","code":"var q = db.Orders.Where(x => x.Total > 100); var list = await q.ToListAsync();","category":"C#","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: IQueryable builds provider-translatable queries, while IEnumerable operates through enumeration.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: IQueryable<T> exposes an expression tree and an EF provider that can translate supported operations to SQL. IEnumerable<T> is an enumeration contract and can be lazy; it does NOT necessarily mean everything is already in memory. ToList executes/materializes; Where after ToList executes in memory. Put Where/Select before ToListAsync.\n\nExample: var q = db.Orders.Where(x => x.Total > 100); var list = await q.ToListAsync();","arabic":"الـIQueryable بيخلي EF يترجم Where وSelect لـSQL قبل التنفيذ. IEnumerable واجهة للتكرار ومش معناها إن البيانات اتحملت بالفعل. لكن ToList بتنفّذ الاستعلام؛ أي Where بعدها هتشتغل داخل التطبيق وهتستهلك نقل وذاكرة أكثر.","commonMistake":"ToList executes/materializes; Where after ToList executes in memory. Put Where/Select before ToListAsync.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in IEnumerable vs IQueryable, and why?","answer":"IQueryable<T> exposes an expression tree and an EF provider that can translate supported operations to SQL. IEnumerable<T> is an enumeration contract and can be lazy; it does NOT necessarily mean everything is already in memory. ToList executes/materializes; Where after ToList executes in memory. Put Where/Select before ToListAsync."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for IEnumerable vs IQueryable.","answer":"الـIQueryable بيخلي EF يترجم Where وSelect لـSQL قبل التنفيذ. IEnumerable واجهة للتكرار ومش معناها إن البيانات اتحملت بالفعل. لكن ToList بتنفّذ الاستعلام؛ أي Where بعدها هتشتغل داخل التطبيق وهتستهلك نقل وذاكرة أكثر."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-4","day":1,"title":"Async · Task.WhenAll","concept":"Start each async operation and await Task.WhenAll.","ar":"لما عندك طلبين HTTP مستقلين، شغّلهم الأول وبعدين await Task.WhenAll لتقليل زمن الانتظار. ماينفعش تعمل عمليتين EF متزامنتين بنفس DbContext لأنه مش thread-safe.","question":"How do you fetch independent data sources concurrently?","answer":"Start each async operation and await Task.WhenAll.","code":"var a = LoadAAsync(); var b = LoadBAsync(); await Task.WhenAll(a,b);","category":"Async","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Start each async operation and await Task.WhenAll.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: Task.WhenAll waits for independently started tasks concurrently, reducing total waiting time for unrelated I/O. It does not start new threads by itself. Exceptions propagate when awaited. EF Core DbContext forbids overlapping operations, so use separate contexts for concurrent database work.\n\nExample: var a = LoadAAsync(); var b = LoadBAsync(); await Task.WhenAll(a,b);","arabic":"لما عندك طلبين HTTP مستقلين، شغّلهم الأول وبعدين await Task.WhenAll لتقليل زمن الانتظار. ماينفعش تعمل عمليتين EF متزامنتين بنفس DbContext لأنه مش thread-safe.","commonMistake":"Exceptions propagate when awaited. EF Core DbContext forbids overlapping operations, so use separate contexts for concurrent database work.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Task.WhenAll, and why?","answer":"Task.WhenAll waits for independently started tasks concurrently, reducing total waiting time for unrelated I/O. It does not start new threads by itself. Exceptions propagate when awaited. EF Core DbContext forbids overlapping operations, so use separate contexts for concurrent database work."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Task.WhenAll.","answer":"لما عندك طلبين HTTP مستقلين، شغّلهم الأول وبعدين await Task.WhenAll لتقليل زمن الانتظار. ماينفعش تعمل عمليتين EF متزامنتين بنفس DbContext لأنه مش thread-safe."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-5","day":1,"title":"Async · CancellationToken","concept":"It lets expensive work stop cooperatively after cancellation.","ar":"لو العميل قفل الاتصال، RequestAborted بيسمح لك تلغي SQL/HTTP work اللي لسه شغال. مرّر الـtoken للطبقات التالية. الإلغاء تعاوني ومش مضمون يوقف العملية فورًا، خصوصًا لو فيه transaction أو external side effect.","question":"Why propagate CancellationToken throughout an API request?","answer":"It lets expensive work stop cooperatively after cancellation.","code":"var item = await db.Items.FirstOrDefaultAsync(x => x.Id == id, ct);","category":"Async","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: It lets expensive work stop cooperatively after cancellation.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: CancellationToken is cooperative, not forced termination. ASP.NET Core supplies HttpContext.RequestAborted; pass it to EF Core, HTTP clients and long-running operations. Cancellation may happen at any await; handle cleanup and avoid claiming a partially completed write succeeded.\n\nExample: var item = await db.Items.FirstOrDefaultAsync(x => x.Id == id, ct);","arabic":"لو العميل قفل الاتصال، RequestAborted بيسمح لك تلغي SQL/HTTP work اللي لسه شغال. مرّر الـtoken للطبقات التالية. الإلغاء تعاوني ومش مضمون يوقف العملية فورًا، خصوصًا لو فيه transaction أو external side effect.","commonMistake":"ASP.NET Core supplies HttpContext.RequestAborted; pass it to EF Core, HTTP clients and long-running operations. Cancellation may happen at any await; handle cleanup and avoid claiming a partially completed write succeeded.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in CancellationToken, and why?","answer":"CancellationToken is cooperative, not forced termination. ASP.NET Core supplies HttpContext.RequestAborted; pass it to EF Core, HTTP clients and long-running operations. Cancellation may happen at any await; handle cleanup and avoid claiming a partially completed write succeeded."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for CancellationToken.","answer":"لو العميل قفل الاتصال، RequestAborted بيسمح لك تلغي SQL/HTTP work اللي لسه شغال. مرّر الـtoken للطبقات التالية. الإلغاء تعاوني ومش مضمون يوقف العملية فورًا، خصوصًا لو فيه transaction أو external side effect."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-6","day":1,"title":"Async · Async locking","concept":"SemaphoreSlim.WaitAsync permits asynchronous waiting without blocking a thread.","ar":"الـlock العادي مش مناسب لجزء فيه await. استخدم SemaphoreSlim.WaitAsync وخلي Release في finally بعد نجاح WaitAsync. مهم: ده بيحمي نفس الـprocess فقط، مش كل الـinstances على servers مختلفة.","question":"Why use SemaphoreSlim instead of lock for async code?","answer":"SemaphoreSlim.WaitAsync permits asynchronous waiting without blocking a thread.","code":"await gate.WaitAsync(ct); try { await WorkAsync(ct); } finally { gate.Release(); }","category":"Async","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: SemaphoreSlim.WaitAsync permits asynchronous waiting without blocking a thread.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: A C# lock cannot contain await in its body because its thread ownership semantics conflict with suspension. SemaphoreSlim.WaitAsync waits without blocking a worker thread; always Release in finally after successfully acquiring it. SemaphoreSlim guards only processes sharing that instance, not distributed servers.\n\nExample: await gate.WaitAsync(ct); try { await WorkAsync(ct); } finally { gate.Release(); }","arabic":"الـlock العادي مش مناسب لجزء فيه await. استخدم SemaphoreSlim.WaitAsync وخلي Release في finally بعد نجاح WaitAsync. مهم: ده بيحمي نفس الـprocess فقط، مش كل الـinstances على servers مختلفة.","commonMistake":"SemaphoreSlim.WaitAsync waits without blocking a worker thread; always Release in finally after successfully acquiring it. SemaphoreSlim guards only processes sharing that instance, not distributed servers.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Async locking, and why?","answer":"A C# lock cannot contain await in its body because its thread ownership semantics conflict with suspension. SemaphoreSlim.WaitAsync waits without blocking a worker thread; always Release in finally after successfully acquiring it. SemaphoreSlim guards only processes sharing that instance, not distributed servers."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Async locking.","answer":"الـlock العادي مش مناسب لجزء فيه await. استخدم SemaphoreSlim.WaitAsync وخلي Release في finally بعد نجاح WaitAsync. مهم: ده بيحمي نفس الـprocess فقط، مش كل الـinstances على servers مختلفة."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-7","day":1,"title":"ASP.NET Core · Scoped services in hosted workers","concept":"Create a DI scope for each unit of work.","ar":"الـBackgroundService Singleton لكن DbContext Scoped. اعمل scope جديد لكل job باستخدام IServiceScopeFactory، وخد منه DbContext وبعد ما الـjob يخلص اتخلص من الـscope. ماتخزنش DbContext طول عمر الـworker.","question":"How should a BackgroundService use a scoped DbContext?","answer":"Create a DI scope for each unit of work.","code":"using var scope = scopeFactory.CreateScope(); var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDbContext>();","category":"ASP.NET Core","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Create a DI scope for each unit of work.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: BackgroundService is registered as a singleton. A DbContext normally has scoped lifetime. Inject IServiceScopeFactory and create a fresh scope for each job/iteration, then resolve and dispose the context inside it. Never keep the resolved DbContext for the entire worker lifetime.\n\nExample: using var scope = scopeFactory.CreateScope(); var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDbContext>();","arabic":"الـBackgroundService Singleton لكن DbContext Scoped. اعمل scope جديد لكل job باستخدام IServiceScopeFactory، وخد منه DbContext وبعد ما الـjob يخلص اتخلص من الـscope. ماتخزنش DbContext طول عمر الـworker.","commonMistake":"Inject IServiceScopeFactory and create a fresh scope for each job/iteration, then resolve and dispose the context inside it. Never keep the resolved DbContext for the entire worker lifetime.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Scoped services in hosted workers, and why?","answer":"BackgroundService is registered as a singleton. A DbContext normally has scoped lifetime. Inject IServiceScopeFactory and create a fresh scope for each job/iteration, then resolve and dispose the context inside it. Never keep the resolved DbContext for the entire worker lifetime."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Scoped services in hosted workers.","answer":"الـBackgroundService Singleton لكن DbContext Scoped. اعمل scope جديد لكل job باستخدام IServiceScopeFactory، وخد منه DbContext وبعد ما الـjob يخلص اتخلص من الـscope. ماتخزنش DbContext طول عمر الـworker."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-8","day":1,"title":"ASP.NET Core · Idempotency for writes","concept":"Store a unique idempotency key and return the prior outcome on retries.","ar":"لو العميل عمل POST للدفع واتأخر الرد، ممكن يعيد نفس الطلب وتحصّل عمليتين. الـIdempotency-Key مع unique constraint ومعاملة SQL بيخلي إعادة نفس الطلب ترجع نفس النتيجة. لازم تتحقق كمان إن نفس الـkey مش مستخدم بpayload مختلف.","question":"How would you prevent duplicate payments when a client retries?","answer":"Store a unique idempotency key and return the prior outcome on retries.","code":"CREATE UNIQUE INDEX UX_PaymentRequest ON Payments(TenantId, RequestKey);","category":"ASP.NET Core","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Store a unique idempotency key and return the prior outcome on retries.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: A client retry after a timeout might repeat a payment or order. Require an idempotency key tied to tenant and request fingerprint, enforce a unique database constraint, persist the result transactionally, and return the same result for duplicate retries. A Redis flag alone can race or expire.\n\nExample: CREATE UNIQUE INDEX UX_PaymentRequest ON Payments(TenantId, RequestKey);","arabic":"لو العميل عمل POST للدفع واتأخر الرد، ممكن يعيد نفس الطلب وتحصّل عمليتين. الـIdempotency-Key مع unique constraint ومعاملة SQL بيخلي إعادة نفس الطلب ترجع نفس النتيجة. لازم تتحقق كمان إن نفس الـkey مش مستخدم بpayload مختلف.","commonMistake":"Require an idempotency key tied to tenant and request fingerprint, enforce a unique database constraint, persist the result transactionally, and return the same result for duplicate retries. A Redis flag alone can race or expire.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Idempotency for writes, and why?","answer":"A client retry after a timeout might repeat a payment or order. Require an idempotency key tied to tenant and request fingerprint, enforce a unique database constraint, persist the result transactionally, and return the same result for duplicate retries. A Redis flag alone can race or expire."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Idempotency for writes.","answer":"لو العميل عمل POST للدفع واتأخر الرد، ممكن يعيد نفس الطلب وتحصّل عمليتين. الـIdempotency-Key مع unique constraint ومعاملة SQL بيخلي إعادة نفس الطلب ترجع نفس النتيجة. لازم تتحقق كمان إن نفس الـkey مش مستخدم بpayload مختلف."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-9","day":1,"title":"Security · JWT validation","concept":"Signature, issuer, audience, expiry and applicable authorization rules.","ar":"الـJWT مجرد string تقدر تفك محتواها بدون ما تثبت صحتها. لازم API يتحقق من signature وissuer وaudience وexpiry، وبعد كده يفحص permissions أو scopes وملكية الـresource. Authentication غير Authorization.","question":"What must an API validate before trusting a JWT?","answer":"Signature, issuer, audience, expiry and applicable authorization rules.","code":"builder.Services.AddAuthentication().AddJwtBearer(o => { o.Authority = issuer; o.Audience = \"api\"; });","category":"Security","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Signature, issuer, audience, expiry and applicable authorization rules.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: JWT is only trusted after verifying a valid signature against trusted keys, allowed signing algorithms, issuer, audience, time claims and token policies. Decoding its base64 payload proves nothing. After authentication, authorization separately checks permissions/roles/scopes and resource ownership.\n\nExample: builder.Services.AddAuthentication().AddJwtBearer(o => { o.Authority = issuer; o.Audience = \"api\"; });","arabic":"الـJWT مجرد string تقدر تفك محتواها بدون ما تثبت صحتها. لازم API يتحقق من signature وissuer وaudience وexpiry، وبعد كده يفحص permissions أو scopes وملكية الـresource. Authentication غير Authorization.","commonMistake":"Decoding its base64 payload proves nothing. After authentication, authorization separately checks permissions/roles/scopes and resource ownership.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in JWT validation, and why?","answer":"JWT is only trusted after verifying a valid signature against trusted keys, allowed signing algorithms, issuer, audience, time claims and token policies. Decoding its base64 payload proves nothing. After authentication, authorization separately checks permissions/roles/scopes and resource ownership."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for JWT validation.","answer":"الـJWT مجرد string تقدر تفك محتواها بدون ما تثبت صحتها. لازم API يتحقق من signature وissuer وaudience وexpiry، وبعد كده يفحص permissions أو scopes وملكية الـresource. Authentication غير Authorization."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-10","day":1,"title":"EF Core · N+1 queries","concept":"Inspect generated SQL and project or eagerly load only necessary related data.","ar":"لو جبت 100 Order وبعدها كل واحد فتح Customer بالـlazy loading، ممكن يحصل 101 SQL query. اعرف ده من SQL logs. استخدم projection بـSelect لو محتاج حقول قليلة أو Include لو محتاج entities كاملة. Include لcollections كثيرة ممكن يكرر rows.","question":"How can you identify and avoid the N+1 query problem?","answer":"Inspect generated SQL and project or eagerly load only necessary related data.","code":"var rows = await db.Orders.Select(o => new {o.Id, Customer=o.Customer.Name}).ToListAsync();","category":"EF Core","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Inspect generated SQL and project or eagerly load only necessary related data.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: N+1 occurs when one query loads N parents and lazy loading causes up to N further child queries. Observe EF command logs or a profiler. Fix with SQL-side Select projection when possible; use Include for needed full graphs. Loading several collections with Include may cause cartesian explosion, where AsSplitQuery can help at the cost of round trips.\n\nExample: var rows = await db.Orders.Select(o => new {o.Id, Customer=o.Customer.Name}).ToListAsync();","arabic":"لو جبت 100 Order وبعدها كل واحد فتح Customer بالـlazy loading، ممكن يحصل 101 SQL query. اعرف ده من SQL logs. استخدم projection بـSelect لو محتاج حقول قليلة أو Include لو محتاج entities كاملة. Include لcollections كثيرة ممكن يكرر rows.","commonMistake":"Fix with SQL-side Select projection when possible; use Include for needed full graphs. Loading several collections with Include may cause cartesian explosion, where AsSplitQuery can help at the cost of round trips.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in N+1 queries, and why?","answer":"N+1 occurs when one query loads N parents and lazy loading causes up to N further child queries. Observe EF command logs or a profiler. Fix with SQL-side Select projection when possible; use Include for needed full graphs. Loading several collections with Include may cause cartesian explosion, where AsSplitQuery can help at the cost of round trips."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for N+1 queries.","answer":"لو جبت 100 Order وبعدها كل واحد فتح Customer بالـlazy loading، ممكن يحصل 101 SQL query. اعرف ده من SQL logs. استخدم projection بـSelect لو محتاج حقول قليلة أو Include لو محتاج entities كاملة. Include لcollections كثيرة ممكن يكرر rows."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-11","day":1,"title":"EF Core · Optimistic concurrency","concept":"Use a concurrency token such as SQL Server rowversion and resolve update conflicts.","ar":"لو مستخدمين فتحوا نفس Order، rowversion بتخلي UPDATE يتأكد إن النسخة ما اتغيرتش. لو اتغيرت، EF بيرمي DbUpdateConcurrencyException بدل overwrite صامت. رجّع 409 واسمح للمستخدم يعيد التعديل بناءً على أحدث بيانات.","question":"How do you handle two users editing the same record?","answer":"Use a concurrency token such as SQL Server rowversion and resolve update conflicts.","code":"builder.Entity<Order>().Property(x => x.RowVersion).IsRowVersion();","category":"EF Core","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Use a concurrency token such as SQL Server rowversion and resolve update conflicts.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: Optimistic concurrency sends the original rowversion as a predicate in UPDATE. If another writer updated the row, no row matches and EF Core raises DbUpdateConcurrencyException. Return a conflict (often HTTP 409) with fresh state or merge intentionally; retries must not discard the other writer's changes.\n\nExample: builder.Entity<Order>().Property(x => x.RowVersion).IsRowVersion();","arabic":"لو مستخدمين فتحوا نفس Order، rowversion بتخلي UPDATE يتأكد إن النسخة ما اتغيرتش. لو اتغيرت، EF بيرمي DbUpdateConcurrencyException بدل overwrite صامت. رجّع 409 واسمح للمستخدم يعيد التعديل بناءً على أحدث بيانات.","commonMistake":"If another writer updated the row, no row matches and EF Core raises DbUpdateConcurrencyException. Return a conflict (often HTTP 409) with fresh state or merge intentionally; retries must not discard the other writer's changes.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Optimistic concurrency, and why?","answer":"Optimistic concurrency sends the original rowversion as a predicate in UPDATE. If another writer updated the row, no row matches and EF Core raises DbUpdateConcurrencyException. Return a conflict (often HTTP 409) with fresh state or merge intentionally; retries must not discard the other writer's changes."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Optimistic concurrency.","answer":"لو مستخدمين فتحوا نفس Order، rowversion بتخلي UPDATE يتأكد إن النسخة ما اتغيرتش. لو اتغيرت، EF بيرمي DbUpdateConcurrencyException بدل overwrite صامت. رجّع 409 واسمح للمستخدم يعيد التعديل بناءً على أحدث بيانات."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-12","day":1,"title":"SQL Server · Window functions","concept":"Use ROW_NUMBER partitioned by customer, ordered by date and a unique tie-breaker.","ar":"الـROW_NUMBER بيقسّم النتائج حسب CustomerId ويرقّم كل مجموعة من الأحدث للأقدم. بعدها تختار rn = 1 علشان أحدث Order لكل عميل. زوّد Id في ORDER BY لأن اتنين Orders ممكن يكون لهم نفس CreatedAt.","question":"How can you select the latest order per customer?","answer":"Use ROW_NUMBER partitioned by customer, ordered by date and a unique tie-breaker.","code":"SELECT * FROM (SELECT o.*, ROW_NUMBER() OVER(PARTITION BY CustomerId ORDER BY CreatedAt DESC, Id DESC) rn FROM Orders o) x WHERE rn=1;","category":"SQL Server","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Use ROW_NUMBER partitioned by customer, ordered by date and a unique tie-breaker.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: ROW_NUMBER() OVER(PARTITION BY CustomerId ORDER BY CreatedAt DESC, Id DESC) numbers orders within each customer group, newest first. Wrap as a CTE/subquery and filter rn = 1. Including Id breaks timestamp ties deterministically. For ties you want to preserve, consider DENSE_RANK instead.\n\nExample: SELECT * FROM (SELECT o.*, ROW_NUMBER() OVER(PARTITION BY CustomerId ORDER BY CreatedAt DESC, Id DESC) rn FROM Orders o) x WHERE rn=1;","arabic":"الـROW_NUMBER بيقسّم النتائج حسب CustomerId ويرقّم كل مجموعة من الأحدث للأقدم. بعدها تختار rn = 1 علشان أحدث Order لكل عميل. زوّد Id في ORDER BY لأن اتنين Orders ممكن يكون لهم نفس CreatedAt.","commonMistake":"Including Id breaks timestamp ties deterministically. For ties you want to preserve, consider DENSE_RANK instead.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Window functions, and why?","answer":"ROW_NUMBER() OVER(PARTITION BY CustomerId ORDER BY CreatedAt DESC, Id DESC) numbers orders within each customer group, newest first. Wrap as a CTE/subquery and filter rn = 1. Including Id breaks timestamp ties deterministically. For ties you want to preserve, consider DENSE_RANK instead."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Window functions.","answer":"الـROW_NUMBER بيقسّم النتائج حسب CustomerId ويرقّم كل مجموعة من الأحدث للأقدم. بعدها تختار rn = 1 علشان أحدث Order لكل عميل. زوّد Id في ORDER BY لأن اتنين Orders ممكن يكون لهم نفس CreatedAt."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-13","day":1,"title":"SQL Server · Covering indexes","concept":"When an index contains the key and included columns required by a frequent query.","ar":"الـCovering Index بيخلي SQL يقرأ من الـindex مباشرة بدون lookup للجدول عشان الأعمدة المطلوبة موجودة. اختار key columns حسب WHERE وORDER BY، وحط أعمدة العرض في INCLUDE. اختبر Actual Execution Plan لأن كل index إضافي بيبطّأ writes.","question":"When is a covering index valuable?","answer":"When an index contains the key and included columns required by a frequent query.","code":"CREATE INDEX IX_Orders_TenantDate ON Orders(TenantId, CreatedAt) INCLUDE(Status);","category":"SQL Server","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: When an index contains the key and included columns required by a frequent query.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: A covering index supplies every requested column via key and INCLUDE columns, avoiding key lookups for a specific query shape. Put equality predicates in leading key columns; use INCLUDE for returned columns not needed for seek/order. Verify plans and logical reads: larger indexes cost storage and write/update overhead.\n\nExample: CREATE INDEX IX_Orders_TenantDate ON Orders(TenantId, CreatedAt) INCLUDE(Status);","arabic":"الـCovering Index بيخلي SQL يقرأ من الـindex مباشرة بدون lookup للجدول عشان الأعمدة المطلوبة موجودة. اختار key columns حسب WHERE وORDER BY، وحط أعمدة العرض في INCLUDE. اختبر Actual Execution Plan لأن كل index إضافي بيبطّأ writes.","commonMistake":"Put equality predicates in leading key columns; use INCLUDE for returned columns not needed for seek/order. Verify plans and logical reads: larger indexes cost storage and write/update overhead.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Covering indexes, and why?","answer":"A covering index supplies every requested column via key and INCLUDE columns, avoiding key lookups for a specific query shape. Put equality predicates in leading key columns; use INCLUDE for returned columns not needed for seek/order. Verify plans and logical reads: larger indexes cost storage and write/update overhead."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Covering indexes.","answer":"الـCovering Index بيخلي SQL يقرأ من الـindex مباشرة بدون lookup للجدول عشان الأعمدة المطلوبة موجودة. اختار key columns حسب WHERE وORDER BY، وحط أعمدة العرض في INCLUDE. اختبر Actual Execution Plan لأن كل index إضافي بيبطّأ writes."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-14","day":1,"title":"SQL Server · Deadlock investigation","concept":"Capture deadlock graphs and examine resource lock ordering.","ar":"الـDeadlock مش مجرد query بطيئة؛ ده انتظار دائري بين معاملات. SQL Server بيختار victim ويرجع error 1205. شوف Deadlock Graph لمعرفة الأقفال والاستعلامات، ووحّد ترتيب التحديثات وقصّر المعاملات. ممكن retry محدود لو العملية آمنة.","question":"How do you diagnose SQL Server deadlocks?","answer":"Capture deadlock graphs and examine resource lock ordering.","code":"-- Inspect deadlock XML from Extended Events.","category":"SQL Server","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Capture deadlock graphs and examine resource lock ordering.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: A deadlock is a circular wait: transaction A holds resource X and waits for Y, while B holds Y and waits for X. SQL Server chooses a victim and returns error 1205. Use Extended Events deadlock graph to find statements and locks. Fix inconsistent lock order, long transactions or missing indexes; apply bounded retries only for safe operations.\n\nExample: -- Inspect deadlock XML from Extended Events.","arabic":"الـDeadlock مش مجرد query بطيئة؛ ده انتظار دائري بين معاملات. SQL Server بيختار victim ويرجع error 1205. شوف Deadlock Graph لمعرفة الأقفال والاستعلامات، ووحّد ترتيب التحديثات وقصّر المعاملات. ممكن retry محدود لو العملية آمنة.","commonMistake":"Use Extended Events deadlock graph to find statements and locks. Fix inconsistent lock order, long transactions or missing indexes; apply bounded retries only for safe operations.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Deadlock investigation, and why?","answer":"A deadlock is a circular wait: transaction A holds resource X and waits for Y, while B holds Y and waits for X. SQL Server chooses a victim and returns error 1205. Use Extended Events deadlock graph to find statements and locks. Fix inconsistent lock order, long transactions or missing indexes; apply bounded retries only for safe operations."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Deadlock investigation.","answer":"الـDeadlock مش مجرد query بطيئة؛ ده انتظار دائري بين معاملات. SQL Server بيختار victim ويرجع error 1205. شوف Deadlock Graph لمعرفة الأقفال والاستعلامات، ووحّد ترتيب التحديثات وقصّر المعاملات. ممكن retry محدود لو العملية آمنة."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-15","day":2,"title":"Angular · RxJS flattening operators","concept":"Use switchMap for latest-result-wins work such as search; mergeMap for independent concurrent work.","ar":"في Search Box استخدم debounceTime ثم switchMap: لما المستخدم يكتب قيمة جديدة، الاشتراك القديم يتلغى وتعرض أحدث نتيجة. mergeMap ينفّذ بالتوازي؛ concatMap بالترتيب؛ exhaustMap يتجاهل الضغطات المتكررة أثناء العملية.","question":"When do you choose switchMap over mergeMap?","answer":"Use switchMap for latest-result-wins work such as search; mergeMap for independent concurrent work.","code":"search$.pipe(debounceTime(250), switchMap(q => api.search(q)));","category":"Angular","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Use switchMap for latest-result-wins work such as search; mergeMap for independent concurrent work.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: switchMap unsubscribes the previous inner observable when a newer source value arrives, ideal for a search box. mergeMap processes inner streams concurrently, concatMap queues them sequentially, and exhaustMap ignores new emissions while one is active. Never blindly use switchMap for payments or writes that must complete.\n\nExample: search$.pipe(debounceTime(250), switchMap(q => api.search(q)));","arabic":"في Search Box استخدم debounceTime ثم switchMap: لما المستخدم يكتب قيمة جديدة، الاشتراك القديم يتلغى وتعرض أحدث نتيجة. mergeMap ينفّذ بالتوازي؛ concatMap بالترتيب؛ exhaustMap يتجاهل الضغطات المتكررة أثناء العملية.","commonMistake":"mergeMap processes inner streams concurrently, concatMap queues them sequentially, and exhaustMap ignores new emissions while one is active. Never blindly use switchMap for payments or writes that must complete.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in RxJS flattening operators, and why?","answer":"switchMap unsubscribes the previous inner observable when a newer source value arrives, ideal for a search box. mergeMap processes inner streams concurrently, concatMap queues them sequentially, and exhaustMap ignores new emissions while one is active. Never blindly use switchMap for payments or writes that must complete."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for RxJS flattening operators.","answer":"في Search Box استخدم debounceTime ثم switchMap: لما المستخدم يكتب قيمة جديدة، الاشتراك القديم يتلغى وتعرض أحدث نتيجة. mergeMap ينفّذ بالتوازي؛ concatMap بالترتيب؛ exhaustMap يتجاهل الضغطات المتكررة أثناء العملية."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-16","day":2,"title":"Angular · OnPush and immutable state","concept":"Mutating an existing input reference may not trigger the expected check.","ar":"لو Child Component OnPush وأنت عدّلت item.name على نفس object، ممكن ماتحصلش check كما تتوقع. اعمل object جديد {...item, name} أو استخدم signals. OnPush مش معناه إنه لا يتحدث مطلقًا؛ events وasync pipe بتشغّل checks.","question":"Why might a component using OnPush not refresh after data mutation?","answer":"Mutating an existing input reference may not trigger the expected check.","code":"@Component({changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush, template:'{{item.name}}'})","category":"Angular","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Mutating an existing input reference may not trigger the expected check.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: OnPush reduces checks by treating input reference updates, template events, async pipe emissions and signal reads as change-notification sources. Mutating a nested property on the same object may not notify a child. Use immutable assignment (new object/array), signals or markForCheck where appropriate.\n\nExample: @Component({changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush, template:'{{item.name}}'})","arabic":"لو Child Component OnPush وأنت عدّلت item.name على نفس object، ممكن ماتحصلش check كما تتوقع. اعمل object جديد {...item, name} أو استخدم signals. OnPush مش معناه إنه لا يتحدث مطلقًا؛ events وasync pipe بتشغّل checks.","commonMistake":"Mutating a nested property on the same object may not notify a child. Use immutable assignment (new object/array), signals or markForCheck where appropriate.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in OnPush and immutable state, and why?","answer":"OnPush reduces checks by treating input reference updates, template events, async pipe emissions and signal reads as change-notification sources. Mutating a nested property on the same object may not notify a child. Use immutable assignment (new object/array), signals or markForCheck where appropriate."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for OnPush and immutable state.","answer":"لو Child Component OnPush وأنت عدّلت item.name على نفس object، ممكن ماتحصلش check كما تتوقع. اعمل object جديد {...item, name} أو استخدم signals. OnPush مش معناه إنه لا يتحدث مطلقًا؛ events وasync pipe بتشغّل checks."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-17","day":2,"title":"Angular · Subscription cleanup","concept":"Use async pipe or takeUntilDestroyed for component-owned subscriptions.","ar":"الـSubject والـinterval ممكن يفضلوا شغالين بعد ما الـcomponent يتدمر، فيحصل memory leak أو duplicate handlers. async pipe أو takeUntilDestroyed بيقفلوا الاشتراك وقت destroy. HttpClient request غالبًا بيكمل لوحده.","question":"How do you avoid long-lived Observable subscriptions leaking?","answer":"Use async pipe or takeUntilDestroyed for component-owned subscriptions.","code":"stream$.pipe(takeUntilDestroyed()).subscribe(console.log);","category":"Angular","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Use async pipe or takeUntilDestroyed for component-owned subscriptions.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: A subscription to a never-ending Subject, interval or event stream can retain component references after navigation. AsyncPipe unsubscribes automatically; takeUntilDestroyed() ties a manual subscription to Angular DestroyRef. Finite HttpClient calls typically complete on their own, though unsubscribing can cancel in-flight requests.\n\nExample: stream$.pipe(takeUntilDestroyed()).subscribe(console.log);","arabic":"الـSubject والـinterval ممكن يفضلوا شغالين بعد ما الـcomponent يتدمر، فيحصل memory leak أو duplicate handlers. async pipe أو takeUntilDestroyed بيقفلوا الاشتراك وقت destroy. HttpClient request غالبًا بيكمل لوحده.","commonMistake":"AsyncPipe unsubscribes automatically; takeUntilDestroyed() ties a manual subscription to Angular DestroyRef. Finite HttpClient calls typically complete on their own, though unsubscribing can cancel in-flight requests.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Subscription cleanup, and why?","answer":"A subscription to a never-ending Subject, interval or event stream can retain component references after navigation. AsyncPipe unsubscribes automatically; takeUntilDestroyed() ties a manual subscription to Angular DestroyRef. Finite HttpClient calls typically complete on their own, though unsubscribing can cancel in-flight requests."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Subscription cleanup.","answer":"الـSubject والـinterval ممكن يفضلوا شغالين بعد ما الـcomponent يتدمر، فيحصل memory leak أو duplicate handlers. async pipe أو takeUntilDestroyed بيقفلوا الاشتراك وقت destroy. HttpClient request غالبًا بيكمل لوحده."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-18","day":2,"title":"Angular · 401 refresh handling","concept":"Retry via a bounded refresh flow, then redirect if refresh fails.","ar":"لو خمس Requests رجعوا 401 في نفس اللحظة، ماتعملش خمس refresh calls. خلّي refresh واحدة مشتركة ثم أعد المحاولات مرة واحدة. لو refresh فشلت، انهي الـsession. ماتدخلش refresh endpoint في retry loop.","question":"How should an HTTP interceptor handle expired access tokens?","answer":"Retry via a bounded refresh flow, then redirect if refresh fails.","code":"// Avoid intercepting the refresh endpoint into an infinite loop.","category":"Angular","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Retry via a bounded refresh flow, then redirect if refresh fails.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: An interceptor can catch 401, initiate refresh once, share that in-flight refresh among simultaneous requests, then retry each original request once with the new access token. Exclude the refresh endpoint to prevent recursion and clear session on failure. Store and transmit refresh tokens using an appropriate secure design.\n\nExample: // Avoid intercepting the refresh endpoint into an infinite loop.","arabic":"لو خمس Requests رجعوا 401 في نفس اللحظة، ماتعملش خمس refresh calls. خلّي refresh واحدة مشتركة ثم أعد المحاولات مرة واحدة. لو refresh فشلت، انهي الـsession. ماتدخلش refresh endpoint في retry loop.","commonMistake":"Exclude the refresh endpoint to prevent recursion and clear session on failure. Store and transmit refresh tokens using an appropriate secure design.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in 401 refresh handling, and why?","answer":"An interceptor can catch 401, initiate refresh once, share that in-flight refresh among simultaneous requests, then retry each original request once with the new access token. Exclude the refresh endpoint to prevent recursion and clear session on failure. Store and transmit refresh tokens using an appropriate secure design."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for 401 refresh handling.","answer":"لو خمس Requests رجعوا 401 في نفس اللحظة، ماتعملش خمس refresh calls. خلّي refresh واحدة مشتركة ثم أعد المحاولات مرة واحدة. لو refresh فشلت، انهي الـsession. ماتدخلش refresh endpoint في retry loop."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-19","day":2,"title":"Redis · Cache stampede","concept":"Use single-flight coordination, TTL jitter and bounded stale reads if acceptable.","ar":"لو Cache Key مهم انتهت صلاحيته، 1000 request ممكن يضربوا SQL مرة واحدة. قلّل ده بـTTL jitter وsingle-flight أو stale-while-revalidate لو مناسب. لازم الـlock ينتهي ويتحقق من المالك؛ غير كده ممكن يحصل congestion جديد.","question":"How do you avoid a surge of database reads after a popular key expires?","answer":"Use single-flight coordination, TTL jitter and bounded stale reads if acceptable.","code":"// key: tenant:{tenantId}:dashboard:v2","category":"Redis","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Use single-flight coordination, TTL jitter and bounded stale reads if acceptable.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: Cache stampede occurs when a hot entry expires and many callers simultaneously regenerate it against the database. Jitter the TTL, coordinate a single regeneration (single-flight), and optionally serve bounded stale data. Locks require expiration, owner verification and fallback so a crashed worker doesn't block everyone.\n\nExample: // key: tenant:{tenantId}:dashboard:v2","arabic":"لو Cache Key مهم انتهت صلاحيته، 1000 request ممكن يضربوا SQL مرة واحدة. قلّل ده بـTTL jitter وsingle-flight أو stale-while-revalidate لو مناسب. لازم الـlock ينتهي ويتحقق من المالك؛ غير كده ممكن يحصل congestion جديد.","commonMistake":"Jitter the TTL, coordinate a single regeneration (single-flight), and optionally serve bounded stale data. Locks require expiration, owner verification and fallback so a crashed worker doesn't block everyone.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Cache stampede, and why?","answer":"Cache stampede occurs when a hot entry expires and many callers simultaneously regenerate it against the database. Jitter the TTL, coordinate a single regeneration (single-flight), and optionally serve bounded stale data. Locks require expiration, owner verification and fallback so a crashed worker doesn't block everyone."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Cache stampede.","answer":"لو Cache Key مهم انتهت صلاحيته، 1000 request ممكن يضربوا SQL مرة واحدة. قلّل ده بـTTL jitter وsingle-flight أو stale-while-revalidate لو مناسب. لازم الـlock ينتهي ويتحقق من المالك؛ غير كده ممكن يحصل congestion جديد."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-20","day":2,"title":"Redis · Distributed lock ownership","concept":"Expiry and process pauses can allow overlapping owners; release must verify a unique token.","ar":"SET NX PX بيدي lease مؤقتة، مش ضمان مطلق. لو السيرفر وقف فترة أطول من TTL، سيرفر تاني ممكن يمسك الـlock والأول يكمل بعد ما يرجع. استخدم unique token مع atomic release، وحماية DB لما صحة البيانات مهمة.","question":"Why is SET NX PX not a complete locking solution?","answer":"Expiry and process pauses can allow overlapping owners; release must verify a unique token.","code":"SET orders-lock unique-token NX PX 15000","category":"Redis","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Expiry and process pauses can allow overlapping owners; release must verify a unique token.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: Redis SET key token NX PX ttl grants a lease, not perfect exclusivity. A process can pause past the lease, resume after another process acquires it, and both may act. Release atomically only if token matches; for strict correctness use fencing tokens or database constraints to reject stale actors.\n\nExample: SET orders-lock unique-token NX PX 15000","arabic":"SET NX PX بيدي lease مؤقتة، مش ضمان مطلق. لو السيرفر وقف فترة أطول من TTL، سيرفر تاني ممكن يمسك الـlock والأول يكمل بعد ما يرجع. استخدم unique token مع atomic release، وحماية DB لما صحة البيانات مهمة.","commonMistake":"A process can pause past the lease, resume after another process acquires it, and both may act. Release atomically only if token matches; for strict correctness use fencing tokens or database constraints to reject stale actors.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Distributed lock ownership, and why?","answer":"Redis SET key token NX PX ttl grants a lease, not perfect exclusivity. A process can pause past the lease, resume after another process acquires it, and both may act. Release atomically only if token matches; for strict correctness use fencing tokens or database constraints to reject stale actors."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Distributed lock ownership.","answer":"SET NX PX بيدي lease مؤقتة، مش ضمان مطلق. لو السيرفر وقف فترة أطول من TTL، سيرفر تاني ممكن يمسك الـlock والأول يكمل بعد ما يرجع. استخدم unique token مع atomic release، وحماية DB لما صحة البيانات مهمة."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-21","day":2,"title":"Redis · Cache invalidation","concept":"Another reader can repopulate the cache with stale data.","ar":"لو مسحت الـcache قبل SQL commit، Request تانية ممكن تقرأ الداتا القديمة وتحطها في Redis من جديد. عادةً اعمل SaveChanges ثم invalidate. لكن لو Redis وقع بعد الـcommit، هتفضل stale data؛ ممكن تستخدم Outbox أو versioned keys.","question":"What can go wrong if you invalidate a cache entry before SQL commit?","answer":"Another reader can repopulate the cache with stale data.","code":"await db.SaveChangesAsync(ct); await cache.RemoveAsync(key,ct);","category":"Redis","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Another reader can repopulate the cache with stale data.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: Invalidating a cache before SQL commit is dangerous: a concurrent reader can fetch the old committed data and refill the entry. Invalidate after commit for simpler cache-aside flows, but notice SQL commit and Redis delete are not atomic. For stricter guarantees use an outbox/invalidation event or versioned keys and monitor failures.\n\nExample: await db.SaveChangesAsync(ct); await cache.RemoveAsync(key,ct);","arabic":"لو مسحت الـcache قبل SQL commit، Request تانية ممكن تقرأ الداتا القديمة وتحطها في Redis من جديد. عادةً اعمل SaveChanges ثم invalidate. لكن لو Redis وقع بعد الـcommit، هتفضل stale data؛ ممكن تستخدم Outbox أو versioned keys.","commonMistake":"Invalidate after commit for simpler cache-aside flows, but notice SQL commit and Redis delete are not atomic. For stricter guarantees use an outbox/invalidation event or versioned keys and monitor failures.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Cache invalidation, and why?","answer":"Invalidating a cache before SQL commit is dangerous: a concurrent reader can fetch the old committed data and refill the entry. Invalidate after commit for simpler cache-aside flows, but notice SQL commit and Redis delete are not atomic. For stricter guarantees use an outbox/invalidation event or versioned keys and monitor failures."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Cache invalidation.","answer":"لو مسحت الـcache قبل SQL commit، Request تانية ممكن تقرأ الداتا القديمة وتحطها في Redis من جديد. عادةً اعمل SaveChanges ثم invalidate. لكن لو Redis وقع بعد الـcommit، هتفضل stale data؛ ممكن تستخدم Outbox أو versioned keys."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-22","day":2,"title":"Multi-Tenancy · Tenant-safe caching","concept":"Using a cache key without a trusted TenantId can mix tenant data.","ar":"في SaaS لو key اسمها invoice:15 بس، شركتين عندهم invoice 15 ممكن يشوفوا بيانات بعض. خلّي المفتاح tenant:{tenantId}:invoice:{id}. خد TenantId من token موثوق وتأكد من authorization حتى عند cache hit.","question":"How can Redis accidentally leak data between companies?","answer":"Using a cache key without a trusted TenantId can mix tenant data.","code":"var key = $\"tenant:{tenantId}:invoice:{invoiceId}\";","category":"Multi-Tenancy","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Using a cache key without a trusted TenantId can mix tenant data.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: Cache keys must include tenant identity (and any other authorization-sensitive scope) to prevent two customers with equal record IDs sharing a cached object. TenantId must come from validated identity or securely bound context, not a caller-controlled header. Check permissions before returning cached data too.\n\nExample: var key = $\"tenant:{tenantId}:invoice:{invoiceId}\";","arabic":"في SaaS لو key اسمها invoice:15 بس، شركتين عندهم invoice 15 ممكن يشوفوا بيانات بعض. خلّي المفتاح tenant:{tenantId}:invoice:{id}. خد TenantId من token موثوق وتأكد من authorization حتى عند cache hit.","commonMistake":"TenantId must come from validated identity or securely bound context, not a caller-controlled header. Check permissions before returning cached data too.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Tenant-safe caching, and why?","answer":"Cache keys must include tenant identity (and any other authorization-sensitive scope) to prevent two customers with equal record IDs sharing a cached object. TenantId must come from validated identity or securely bound context, not a caller-controlled header. Check permissions before returning cached data too."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Tenant-safe caching.","answer":"في SaaS لو key اسمها invoice:15 بس، شركتين عندهم invoice 15 ممكن يشوفوا بيانات بعض. خلّي المفتاح tenant:{tenantId}:invoice:{id}. خد TenantId من token موثوق وتأكد من authorization حتى عند cache hit."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-23","day":2,"title":"Multi-Tenancy · Global query filter bypass","concept":"No, raw SQL, IgnoreQueryFilters and privileged paths can bypass them.","ar":"HasQueryFilter بيضيف TenantId تلقائيًا في استعلامات EF المعتادة، لكنه مش حماية كافية لو استخدمت IgnoreQueryFilters أو Raw SQL. تحقق من tenant في services والwrites والbackground jobs. اختبر إن مستخدم شركة A مايقدرش يشوف أو يغير بيانات B.","question":"Are EF Core global filters enough to guarantee isolation?","answer":"No, raw SQL, IgnoreQueryFilters and privileged paths can bypass them.","code":"modelBuilder.Entity<Order>().HasQueryFilter(o => o.TenantId == tenantId);","category":"Multi-Tenancy","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: No, raw SQL, IgnoreQueryFilters and privileged paths can bypass them.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: Global query filters are a useful default predicate, not a security boundary. IgnoreQueryFilters(), direct SQL, bulk jobs, incorrectly scoped tenant providers and writes can bypass isolation. Enforce tenant constraints for reads and writes, test cross-tenant access and consider DB row-level security for stronger defense.\n\nExample: modelBuilder.Entity<Order>().HasQueryFilter(o => o.TenantId == tenantId);","arabic":"HasQueryFilter بيضيف TenantId تلقائيًا في استعلامات EF المعتادة، لكنه مش حماية كافية لو استخدمت IgnoreQueryFilters أو Raw SQL. تحقق من tenant في services والwrites والbackground jobs. اختبر إن مستخدم شركة A مايقدرش يشوف أو يغير بيانات B.","commonMistake":"IgnoreQueryFilters(), direct SQL, bulk jobs, incorrectly scoped tenant providers and writes can bypass isolation. Enforce tenant constraints for reads and writes, test cross-tenant access and consider DB row-level security for stronger defense.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Global query filter bypass, and why?","answer":"Global query filters are a useful default predicate, not a security boundary. IgnoreQueryFilters(), direct SQL, bulk jobs, incorrectly scoped tenant providers and writes can bypass isolation. Enforce tenant constraints for reads and writes, test cross-tenant access and consider DB row-level security for stronger defense."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Global query filter bypass.","answer":"HasQueryFilter بيضيف TenantId تلقائيًا في استعلامات EF المعتادة، لكنه مش حماية كافية لو استخدمت IgnoreQueryFilters أو Raw SQL. تحقق من tenant في services والwrites والbackground jobs. اختبر إن مستخدم شركة A مايقدرش يشوف أو يغير بيانات B."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-24","day":2,"title":"Multi-Tenancy · Database-per-tenant migrations","concept":"Batch, version, observe and resume per-tenant migrations.","ar":"لو عندك مئات Databases، ماتعملش Migration لكلهم دفعة واحدة. شغّل batches وسجّل schema version لكل tenant وحالة النجاح والفشل. لازم الكود يتحمل وجود tenants على نسخ مختلفة خلال rollout لحد ما الكل يكتمل.","question":"How do you roll out schema changes to hundreds of tenant databases?","answer":"Batch, version, observe and resume per-tenant migrations.","code":"// Track tenant schema versions in a control database.","category":"Multi-Tenancy","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Batch, version, observe and resume per-tenant migrations.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: For database-per-tenant SaaS, enumerate tenants from a control database, execute schema migrations in small batches, track each tenant's schema version and status, and resume failed migrations. Deploy code compatible with both old/new schema during rollout. Protect DB capacity and provide rollback/forward-fix strategy.\n\nExample: // Track tenant schema versions in a control database.","arabic":"لو عندك مئات Databases، ماتعملش Migration لكلهم دفعة واحدة. شغّل batches وسجّل schema version لكل tenant وحالة النجاح والفشل. لازم الكود يتحمل وجود tenants على نسخ مختلفة خلال rollout لحد ما الكل يكتمل.","commonMistake":"Deploy code compatible with both old/new schema during rollout. Protect DB capacity and provide rollback/forward-fix strategy.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Database-per-tenant migrations, and why?","answer":"For database-per-tenant SaaS, enumerate tenants from a control database, execute schema migrations in small batches, track each tenant's schema version and status, and resume failed migrations. Deploy code compatible with both old/new schema during rollout. Protect DB capacity and provide rollback/forward-fix strategy."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Database-per-tenant migrations.","answer":"لو عندك مئات Databases، ماتعملش Migration لكلهم دفعة واحدة. شغّل batches وسجّل schema version لكل tenant وحالة النجاح والفشل. لازم الكود يتحمل وجود tenants على نسخ مختلفة خلال rollout لحد ما الكل يكتمل."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-25","day":2,"title":"Architecture · Transactional outbox","concept":"Save the business row and outbox event in the same SQL transaction.","ar":"لو Save Order نجح لكن إرسال رسالة Kafka فشل، الـevent ممكن تضيع. Outbox بتحفظ Order وevent في نفس SQL transaction. Worker بعدين يبعثها مع retry. لأن الرسالة ممكن تتبعت مرتين، الـconsumer لازم يبقى idempotent.","question":"How do you avoid losing an event after a database commit?","answer":"Save the business row and outbox event in the same SQL transaction.","code":"// Insert order and outbox message atomically; publish later.","category":"Architecture","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Save the business row and outbox event in the same SQL transaction.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: A transactional outbox writes the domain change and a pending event to the same SQL transaction. A dispatcher publishes pending events and marks them delivered. Crashes between publish and acknowledgement may cause duplicate delivery, so consumers must be idempotent and failures retried with monitoring.\n\nExample: // Insert order and outbox message atomically; publish later.","arabic":"لو Save Order نجح لكن إرسال رسالة Kafka فشل، الـevent ممكن تضيع. Outbox بتحفظ Order وevent في نفس SQL transaction. Worker بعدين يبعثها مع retry. لأن الرسالة ممكن تتبعت مرتين، الـconsumer لازم يبقى idempotent.","commonMistake":"A dispatcher publishes pending events and marks them delivered. Crashes between publish and acknowledgement may cause duplicate delivery, so consumers must be idempotent and failures retried with monitoring.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Transactional outbox, and why?","answer":"A transactional outbox writes the domain change and a pending event to the same SQL transaction. A dispatcher publishes pending events and marks them delivered. Crashes between publish and acknowledgement may cause duplicate delivery, so consumers must be idempotent and failures retried with monitoring."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Transactional outbox.","answer":"لو Save Order نجح لكن إرسال رسالة Kafka فشل، الـevent ممكن تضيع. Outbox بتحفظ Order وevent في نفس SQL transaction. Worker بعدين يبعثها مع retry. لأن الرسالة ممكن تتبعت مرتين، الـconsumer لازم يبقى idempotent."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-26","day":3,"title":"SignalR · Multiple server instances","concept":"A supported scale-out mechanism such as a Redis backplane or managed SignalR service.","ar":"لما SignalR شغال على أكتر من instance، المستخدم المتصل بالسيرفر B لازم توصله رسالة مصدرها السيرفر A. Redis Backplane أو managed SignalR service بيوزّع الرسائل. لكن offline notifications محتاجة DB أو queue لأنها مش محفوظة تلقائيًا.","question":"What do you need when SignalR clients connect to different app instances?","answer":"A supported scale-out mechanism such as a Redis backplane or managed SignalR service.","code":"builder.Services.AddSignalR().AddStackExchangeRedis(connection);","category":"SignalR","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: A supported scale-out mechanism such as a Redis backplane or managed SignalR service.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: SignalR maintains connections on the app instance they reached. With multiple nodes, messages targeted to connections on other nodes require a supported backplane such as Redis or a managed SignalR service. Configure affinity/transport appropriately. A backplane does not retain messages for offline clients; persist those separately.\n\nExample: builder.Services.AddSignalR().AddStackExchangeRedis(connection);","arabic":"لما SignalR شغال على أكتر من instance، المستخدم المتصل بالسيرفر B لازم توصله رسالة مصدرها السيرفر A. Redis Backplane أو managed SignalR service بيوزّع الرسائل. لكن offline notifications محتاجة DB أو queue لأنها مش محفوظة تلقائيًا.","commonMistake":"Configure affinity/transport appropriately. A backplane does not retain messages for offline clients; persist those separately.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Multiple server instances, and why?","answer":"SignalR maintains connections on the app instance they reached. With multiple nodes, messages targeted to connections on other nodes require a supported backplane such as Redis or a managed SignalR service. Configure affinity/transport appropriately. A backplane does not retain messages for offline clients; persist those separately."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Multiple server instances.","answer":"لما SignalR شغال على أكتر من instance، المستخدم المتصل بالسيرفر B لازم توصله رسالة مصدرها السيرفر A. Redis Backplane أو managed SignalR service بيوزّع الرسائل. لكن offline notifications محتاجة DB أو queue لأنها مش محفوظة تلقائيًا."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-27","day":3,"title":"Testing · Integration test realism","concept":"It exercises routing, serialization, middleware, DI and authentication.","ar":"Unit Test للـcontroller مش هيكشف مشاكل routing أو middleware أو serialization. WebApplicationFactory بيشغّل API pipeline شبه الحقيقي. اختبر status code وJSON والتغييرات في DB، واستخدم خدمات وDatabase مخصصة للاختبار.","question":"Why use WebApplicationFactory instead of testing a controller method alone?","answer":"It exercises routing, serialization, middleware, DI and authentication.","code":"var client = factory.CreateClient(); var res = await client.GetAsync(\"/api/orders\");","category":"Testing","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: It exercises routing, serialization, middleware, DI and authentication.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: WebApplicationFactory boots the ASP.NET Core hosting pipeline in tests so routing, filters, DI, middleware, authentication and serialization are exercised together. Replace external integrations and use isolated test DB. Assert status, response JSON and state changes, unlike a controller unit test with mocked dependencies.\n\nExample: var client = factory.CreateClient(); var res = await client.GetAsync(\"/api/orders\");","arabic":"Unit Test للـcontroller مش هيكشف مشاكل routing أو middleware أو serialization. WebApplicationFactory بيشغّل API pipeline شبه الحقيقي. اختبر status code وJSON والتغييرات في DB، واستخدم خدمات وDatabase مخصصة للاختبار.","commonMistake":"Replace external integrations and use isolated test DB. Assert status, response JSON and state changes, unlike a controller unit test with mocked dependencies.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Integration test realism, and why?","answer":"WebApplicationFactory boots the ASP.NET Core hosting pipeline in tests so routing, filters, DI, middleware, authentication and serialization are exercised together. Replace external integrations and use isolated test DB. Assert status, response JSON and state changes, unlike a controller unit test with mocked dependencies."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Integration test realism.","answer":"Unit Test للـcontroller مش هيكشف مشاكل routing أو middleware أو serialization. WebApplicationFactory بيشغّل API pipeline شبه الحقيقي. اختبر status code وJSON والتغييرات في DB، واستخدم خدمات وDatabase مخصصة للاختبار."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-28","day":3,"title":"Testing · SQL Testcontainers","concept":"It does not reproduce relational constraints, SQL translation or real transactions.","ar":"EF InMemory ممكن يخلي Tests تنجح رغم إن query هتفشل في SQL Server، لأنه لا يطابق constraints وSQL translation. Testcontainers بيشغّل SQL Server حقيقي مؤقت في Docker. أفضل لاختبارات migrations وconcurrency وcomplex queries.","question":"Why can EF Core InMemory give false confidence?","answer":"It does not reproduce relational constraints, SQL translation or real transactions.","code":"// Integration test: spin up disposable SQL Server / Redis.","category":"Testing","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: It does not reproduce relational constraints, SQL translation or real transactions.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: EF Core InMemory is not a relational database: SQL translation, foreign-key constraints, transactions and provider-specific functions can behave differently. For database-critical integration tests, Testcontainers can run real SQL Server with a disposable instance. It improves realism at the cost of slower setup and Docker requirements.\n\nExample: // Integration test: spin up disposable SQL Server / Redis.","arabic":"EF InMemory ممكن يخلي Tests تنجح رغم إن query هتفشل في SQL Server، لأنه لا يطابق constraints وSQL translation. Testcontainers بيشغّل SQL Server حقيقي مؤقت في Docker. أفضل لاختبارات migrations وconcurrency وcomplex queries.","commonMistake":"For database-critical integration tests, Testcontainers can run real SQL Server with a disposable instance. It improves realism at the cost of slower setup and Docker requirements.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in SQL Testcontainers, and why?","answer":"EF Core InMemory is not a relational database: SQL translation, foreign-key constraints, transactions and provider-specific functions can behave differently. For database-critical integration tests, Testcontainers can run real SQL Server with a disposable instance. It improves realism at the cost of slower setup and Docker requirements."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for SQL Testcontainers.","answer":"EF InMemory ممكن يخلي Tests تنجح رغم إن query هتفشل في SQL Server، لأنه لا يطابق constraints وSQL translation. Testcontainers بيشغّل SQL Server حقيقي مؤقت في Docker. أفضل لاختبارات migrations وconcurrency وcomplex queries."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-29","day":3,"title":"System Design · Per-tenant rate limiting","concept":"Partition quotas by authenticated tenant, not untrusted headers.","ar":"في Multi-Tenant SaaS شركة واحدة ممكن تستهلك موارد كل الشركات. اعمل Rate Limiting مبني على TenantId الموثوق، وحدد burst وحد يومي أو بالدقيقة. أرجع 429 وRetry-After، وانتبه إن limits المحلية مش مشتركة بين servers.","question":"How do you protect shared infrastructure from one noisy tenant?","answer":"Partition quotas by authenticated tenant, not untrusted headers.","code":"// Partition rate limiter using trusted tenant identifier.","category":"System Design","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Partition quotas by authenticated tenant, not untrusted headers.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: Rate-limit per authenticated tenant to stop one noisy tenant from exhausting shared CPU, SQL pools or third-party quotas. Design token-bucket/fixed/sliding-window limits with burst budgets and 429 Retry-After. If you have multiple API instances, use coordinated/distributed counters; an in-memory limiter is per instance.\n\nExample: // Partition rate limiter using trusted tenant identifier.","arabic":"في Multi-Tenant SaaS شركة واحدة ممكن تستهلك موارد كل الشركات. اعمل Rate Limiting مبني على TenantId الموثوق، وحدد burst وحد يومي أو بالدقيقة. أرجع 429 وRetry-After، وانتبه إن limits المحلية مش مشتركة بين servers.","commonMistake":"Design token-bucket/fixed/sliding-window limits with burst budgets and 429 Retry-After. If you have multiple API instances, use coordinated/distributed counters; an in-memory limiter is per instance.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Per-tenant rate limiting, and why?","answer":"Rate-limit per authenticated tenant to stop one noisy tenant from exhausting shared CPU, SQL pools or third-party quotas. Design token-bucket/fixed/sliding-window limits with burst budgets and 429 Retry-After. If you have multiple API instances, use coordinated/distributed counters; an in-memory limiter is per instance."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Per-tenant rate limiting.","answer":"في Multi-Tenant SaaS شركة واحدة ممكن تستهلك موارد كل الشركات. اعمل Rate Limiting مبني على TenantId الموثوق، وحدد burst وحد يومي أو بالدقيقة. أرجع 429 وRetry-After، وانتبه إن limits المحلية مش مشتركة بين servers."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-30","day":3,"title":"System Design · Correlation IDs and traces","concept":"Propagate trace context and correlate structured logs and telemetry.","ar":"لو request دخل API وبعدها SQL وBackground Job، TraceId واحد يساعدك تتبع الخطوات والزمن والأخطاء في logs وtraces. استخدم Activity/OpenTelemetry والـstructured logging. ماتسجّلش tokens أو بيانات حساسة.","question":"How do you trace one user request across API and background jobs?","answer":"Propagate trace context and correlate structured logs and telemetry.","code":"var traceId = Activity.Current?.TraceId.ToString();","category":"System Design","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Propagate trace context and correlate structured logs and telemetry.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: Distributed tracing associates request spans, SQL calls and background work under a trace ID, often through W3C trace context and OpenTelemetry. Structured logs should include trace/span IDs; latency percentiles and errors reveal bottlenecks. Propagate context through queues explicitly and never log secrets.\n\nExample: var traceId = Activity.Current?.TraceId.ToString();","arabic":"لو request دخل API وبعدها SQL وBackground Job، TraceId واحد يساعدك تتبع الخطوات والزمن والأخطاء في logs وtraces. استخدم Activity/OpenTelemetry والـstructured logging. ماتسجّلش tokens أو بيانات حساسة.","commonMistake":"Structured logs should include trace/span IDs; latency percentiles and errors reveal bottlenecks. Propagate context through queues explicitly and never log secrets.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Correlation IDs and traces, and why?","answer":"Distributed tracing associates request spans, SQL calls and background work under a trace ID, often through W3C trace context and OpenTelemetry. Structured logs should include trace/span IDs; latency percentiles and errors reveal bottlenecks. Propagate context through queues explicitly and never log secrets."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Correlation IDs and traces.","answer":"لو request دخل API وبعدها SQL وBackground Job، TraceId واحد يساعدك تتبع الخطوات والزمن والأخطاء في logs وtraces. استخدم Activity/OpenTelemetry والـstructured logging. ماتسجّلش tokens أو بيانات حساسة."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-31","day":3,"title":"Coding · Keyset pagination","concept":"Stable ordered cursors avoid offsets shifting during inserts.","ar":"OFFSET 100000 بيخلي SQL يتخطى rows كتيرة، ومع إضافة بيانات أثناء التصفح ممكن يحصل تكرار أو فقد عناصر. Keyset بيكمل من آخر CreatedAt وId شفتهم. لازم ORDER BY ثابت وId tie-breaker مع index مناسب.","question":"Why is cursor pagination sometimes better than OFFSET?","answer":"Stable ordered cursors avoid offsets shifting during inserts.","code":"SELECT TOP 20 * FROM Orders WHERE CreatedAt < @cursorDate ORDER BY CreatedAt DESC;","category":"Coding","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: Stable ordered cursors avoid offsets shifting during inserts.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: OFFSET pagination gets slower on deep pages and can skip/repeat rows if new data arrives. Keyset pagination seeks after a stable cursor using a composite tuple such as (CreatedAt, Id). Order by CreatedAt DESC, Id DESC and filter earlier tuple values. A supporting composite index matters.\n\nExample: SELECT TOP 20 * FROM Orders WHERE CreatedAt < @cursorDate ORDER BY CreatedAt DESC;","arabic":"OFFSET 100000 بيخلي SQL يتخطى rows كتيرة، ومع إضافة بيانات أثناء التصفح ممكن يحصل تكرار أو فقد عناصر. Keyset بيكمل من آخر CreatedAt وId شفتهم. لازم ORDER BY ثابت وId tie-breaker مع index مناسب.","commonMistake":"Order by CreatedAt DESC, Id DESC and filter earlier tuple values. A supporting composite index matters.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in Keyset pagination, and why?","answer":"OFFSET pagination gets slower on deep pages and can skip/repeat rows if new data arrives. Keyset pagination seeks after a stable cursor using a composite tuple such as (CreatedAt, Id). Order by CreatedAt DESC, Id DESC and filter earlier tuple values. A supporting composite index matters."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for Keyset pagination.","answer":"OFFSET 100000 بيخلي SQL يتخطى rows كتيرة، ومع إضافة بيانات أثناء التصفح ممكن يحصل تكرار أو فقد عناصر. Keyset بيكمل من آخر CreatedAt وId شفتهم. لازم ORDER BY ثابت وId tie-breaker مع index مناسب."}]},{"id":"revision-extra-32","day":3,"title":"Coding · HashSet duplicate detection","concept":"A HashSet provides average O(n) time with O(n) additional space.","ar":"للكشف عن duplicate في int array، مرّ على العناصر وخزّنهم في HashSet. أول Add ترجع false معناها العنصر موجود. متوسط الوقت O(n) والذاكرة O(n). البديل sorting لكنه O(n log n) وقد يغيّر ترتيب العناصر.","question":"What is an efficient way to detect duplicates in an array?","answer":"A HashSet provides average O(n) time with O(n) additional space.","code":"bool Dup(int[] a){var s=new HashSet<int>();foreach(var x in a)if(!s.Add(x))return true;return false;}","category":"Coding","detailed":"Definition and correct answer: A HashSet provides average O(n) time with O(n) additional space.\n\nHow it works and real-world trade-offs: A HashSet<T>.Add returns false if the element is already present, so one scan detects duplicates in average O(n) time using up to O(n) extra memory. Sorting can reduce auxiliary space depending on algorithm but usually costs O(n log n) time and may mutate the array.\n\nExample: bool Dup(int[] a){var s=new HashSet<int>();foreach(var x in a)if(!s.Add(x))return true;return false;}","arabic":"للكشف عن duplicate في int array، مرّ على العناصر وخزّنهم في HashSet. أول Add ترجع false معناها العنصر موجود. متوسط الوقت O(n) والذاكرة O(n). البديل sorting لكنه O(n log n) وقد يغيّر ترتيب العناصر.","commonMistake":"A HashSet<T>.Add returns false if the element is already present, so one scan detects duplicates in average O(n) time using up to O(n) extra memory. Sorting can reduce auxiliary space depending on algorithm but usually costs O(n log n) time and may mutate the array.","followUps":[{"question":"What happens internally in HashSet duplicate detection, and why?","answer":"A HashSet<T>.Add returns false if the element is already present, so one scan detects duplicates in average O(n) time using up to O(n) extra memory. Sorting can reduce auxiliary space depending on algorithm but usually costs O(n log n) time and may mutate the array."},{"question":"Explain a practical failure case and mitigation for HashSet duplicate detection.","answer":"للكشف عن duplicate في int array، مرّ على العناصر وخزّنهم في HashSet. أول Add ترجع false معناها العنصر موجود. متوسط الوقت O(n) والذاكرة O(n). البديل sorting لكنه O(n log n) وقد يغيّر ترتيب العناصر."}]}]); render(); }
